&lt;h2 style=&quot;color: #0000ee;&quot;&gt;Supply Chain Lead&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Icarus is hiring a Supply Chain Lead to build and own the supply chain that keeps a fast-moving aerospace startup building and flying.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a critical early hire. You will define the strategy, build the function, and make sure the right parts, materials, and flight hardware are always in the building the moment the team needs them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will own sourcing, procurement, supplier management, inventory, and logistics end to end, and build the organization and systems that let us scale from prototype builds to high-rate production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a wartime supply chain role. Long lead times, single-source risk, and supplier delays cannot be allowed to slow down flight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will operate across the factory floor, engineering, manufacturing, finance, and our supplier base, working directly with the CEO and leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role has the potential to grow into broader operations and supply chain leadership as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;color: #0000ee;&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the supply chain end to end: sourcing, procurement, supplier management, inventory, materials planning, and logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the supply chain strategy as Icarus scales across the full lifecycle — from low-rate prototype builds to high-rate production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the supply chain organization: structure, roles, hiring, and the operating cadence to run it as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a network of high-performing suppliers for flight hardware across avionics, electronics, structures and composites, solar, energy storage, mechanical, and RF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attack long-lead and single-source risk before it becomes a flight blocker. Build buffer, qualify second sources, and stay ahead of demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive make-vs-buy and vertical integration decisions together with engineering and manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the systems, KPIs, and end-to-end visibility (ERP/MRP, receiving, incoming inspection) that let the company see and control its material flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate pricing, terms, and lead times with suppliers, and own PO and vendor management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own supply chain export-control and compliance posture for a defense aerospace company: country-of-origin and domestic sourcing requirements, counterfeit-part avoidance, and supplier quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;color: #0000ee;&quot;&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an elite operator. You get parts in the door and you get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are organized, intense, low-ego, and allergic to bureaucracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can operate at 60,000 feet and on the factory floor in the same day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep experience in supply chain, sourcing, or procurement for complex hardware, and you have owned a supply base and beaten lead times on hard-to-source parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have taken a product from development or prototype into production and scaled the supply chain to match.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are hands-on with ERP/MRP and the systems and KPIs that give a company end-to-end material visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can build not just a supply chain, but a supply chain team and operating cadence, without slowing the company down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have extremely high ownership. When a part is late, you fix it. When a supplier is a risk, you replace them. When something is moving too slowly, you accelerate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You do not need hand-holding. You find the problem, create the plan, and drive it to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working directly with the CEO and senior technical leaders, and making decisions with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
